From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a launcher offers the applications installed

Registers a member of the control protocol that answers a question, the
third after searchFiles() and previewFile(): DomicileHost.searchApps() goes
down with words, and an `apps` event comes back with the desktop entries they
matched -- each a DomicileDesktopEntry carrying its id, name, comment and the
argv it runs, for spawn().

Three lists Chromium owns, and nothing else. The method, the event, its init
dictionary and the entry interface are new files under src/; what cannot be a
new file is a name in a generated-bindings list.

Words, like searchFiles(): which directories hold the desktop entries is the
compositor's to read, and nothing here names one.
---
 .../blink/renderer/bindings/generated_in_modules.gni        | 6 ++++++
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_modules.gni      | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

